Z||000010||GT-maniac||06-16-2001||01:16 AM||||It's kinda funny your situation is the exact opposite of mine. Only in my case I bought a fully loaded 87 GT that I was originally going to use for parts and have now decided to restore. My daily driver is a notchback 85 GT. If the frame is still in decent shape I would try and restore it or maybe make it into a project car. You got it cheap enough that you could probably mod it up and still not have to spend too much on it. Maybe use it for a winter driver and keep your fastback GT safe. I still haven't decided what I'm going to do with two fieros as I don't want to risk either of them to icy winter conditions up here in the far north. ||||reg||1
